WEBVTT

01:36.539 --> 01:39.920
[NORTHWARD]

01:40.060 --> 01:41.750
[Episode 13]

01:42.460 --> 01:43.430
You know what?

01:43.870 --> 01:45.810
Wanghe's trip to Beijing wasn't in vain.

01:46.070 --> 01:47.430
He's actually changed his ways.

01:47.520 --> 01:48.030
Really?

01:48.750 --> 01:50.229
He's studying so diligently now.

01:50.340 --> 01:52.030
He's been studying until midnight every day.

01:52.450 --> 01:54.050
I don't know what's gotten into him.

01:54.950 --> 01:55.830
He went to Beijing and

01:55.870 --> 01:57.190
visited Zhongguancun,

01:57.590 --> 01:58.150
which was eye-opening.

01:58.180 --> 01:59.590
Now he feels he's not good enough.

02:00.330 --> 02:01.160
How do you know?

02:01.290 --> 02:02.220
Did he tell you that?

02:03.950 --> 02:05.530
Why does he tell you everything?

02:06.230 --> 02:08.340
He rolls his eyes whenever I ask him anything.

02:09.030 --> 02:09.669
He needs a good beating.

02:10.550 --> 02:12.760
But you always start arguing with him before he can say much.

02:12.790 --> 02:14.790
Who would want to confide in you then?

02:15.740 --> 02:17.560
He listens when you talk,

02:17.780 --> 02:19.160
and you listen when he talks.

02:19.390 --> 02:20.530
It's a different scenario with me.

02:21.190 --> 02:22.310
Whatever I say,

02:22.450 --> 02:23.930
he always argues back.

02:23.950 --> 02:25.440
He's really nice to you, don't you think?

02:26.780 --> 02:28.180
How is he nice to me?

02:28.540 --> 02:30.079
All he does is piss me off.

02:40.070 --> 02:41.550
Didn't she go out of town to film a movie?

03:00.400 --> 03:04.430
♫At moonset cry the crows♫

03:01.590 --> 03:03.200
Grandpa, you scared me.

03:05.580 --> 03:07.180
What? Did you go to the Internet cafe again?

03:10.330 --> 03:11.630
Wow, you got a lot of nice stuff.

03:11.550 --> 03:14.820
♫Streaking the frosty sky♫

03:11.630 --> 03:13.070
There's a lot more.

03:13.470 --> 03:14.350
Alright, you carry on then.

03:14.380 --> 03:15.180
I'll head inside.

03:15.180 --> 03:16.550
Don't go yet.

03:18.530 --> 03:19.510
Stay here and chat with me for a while.

03:21.390 --> 03:22.110
What happened?

03:22.750 --> 03:26.350
♫Dimly lit fishing boats♫

03:24.140 --> 03:25.650
Your mother just came home.

03:31.300 --> 03:35.570
♫Sadly lie beneath maples♫

03:31.380 --> 03:32.270
Why didn't you tell me

03:32.270 --> 03:33.430
you were coming back beforehand?

03:33.430 --> 03:35.110
I would have picked you up.

03:35.950 --> 03:38.070
You haven't eaten, have you? I'll make you a bowl of noodles.

03:38.070 --> 03:39.590
I ate on the plane.

03:40.030 --> 03:40.840
You've eaten?

03:43.150 --> 03:45.470
What delicious food can there be on a plane?

03:53.190 --> 03:54.400
I heard that

03:55.030 --> 03:56.220
you didn't pass the audition for that show, huh?

03:58.660 --> 04:00.040
The director has no taste.

04:00.530 --> 04:02.290
He cast some young vixen.

04:02.630 --> 04:03.740
I can tell she can't act at a glance.

04:03.770 --> 04:04.940
Once they start filming,

04:04.960 --> 04:05.980
I guarantee he'll regret it.

04:06.510 --> 04:07.590
What kind of director is that?

04:09.440 --> 04:10.710
This show is definitely not going to be good.

04:10.860 --> 04:13.190
When the time comes, I'll inform everyone on Flower Street

04:13.190 --> 04:14.210
not to watch it.

04:14.800 --> 04:16.079
We'll make sure it gets low ratings.

04:19.860 --> 04:21.490
So you're not leaving again this time, right?

04:30.440 --> 04:31.800
Are there other shows you're auditioning for?

04:34.390 --> 04:35.430
No.

04:36.070 --> 04:36.950
It's Ai Linlin.

04:37.750 --> 04:39.000
She has a friend

04:39.390 --> 04:40.630
who left the TV station

04:40.670 --> 04:42.230
and started his own film production company.

04:42.590 --> 04:43.310
They need a producer.

04:46.120 --> 04:47.190
What does that mean? So...

04:47.930 --> 04:49.070
You're going to be a producer?

04:50.630 --> 04:52.510
But you're an actress. You...

04:55.110 --> 04:55.810
Zhimei.

04:56.070 --> 04:56.830
Look.

04:56.950 --> 04:57.870
You love acting,

04:57.950 --> 04:58.670
and I support you.

04:58.670 --> 05:00.390
You can go act, right?

05:01.070 --> 05:01.830
But being a producer

05:01.860 --> 05:03.710
is not something you can just do casually, right?

05:04.070 --> 05:05.350
Think about all the money spent,

05:05.680 --> 05:06.670
with such a large crew

05:06.790 --> 05:07.510
and so many people involved.

05:07.870 --> 05:08.870
What if it can't be aired?

05:09.270 --> 05:10.590
What if the company loses money?

05:11.030 --> 05:12.030
We won't be able to bear that responsibility.

05:12.060 --> 05:12.510
So you...

05:12.630 --> 05:13.670
You can't be a producer.

05:13.970 --> 05:15.500
It's not that serious.

05:15.870 --> 05:16.960
Let me just give it a try.

05:17.190 --> 05:18.400
Maybe it'll work out.

05:18.510 --> 05:20.590
A producer needs social experience.

05:20.670 --> 05:22.140
I think I can do it.

05:22.380 --> 05:23.910
As long as I stay in this industry,

05:24.270 --> 05:26.150
there will always be opportunities to act in the future.

05:26.820 --> 05:27.930
Don't worry about it.

05:29.610 --> 05:32.820
♫Streaking the frosty sky♫

05:29.680 --> 05:30.290
Grandpa.

05:31.400 --> 05:32.320
Tell me,

05:32.870 --> 05:35.670
why does my mom always want to leave home?

05:37.940 --> 05:38.870
Don't you also want to?

05:40.270 --> 05:43.880
♫Dimly lit fishing boats♫

05:41.890 --> 05:44.550
You're so young, yet you're already thinking about

05:45.030 --> 05:46.159
going to Beijing

05:46.230 --> 05:47.700
or Shenzhen.

05:48.970 --> 05:54.940
♫Sadly lie beneath maples♫

05:50.240 --> 05:51.570
Your mom is the same.

05:52.230 --> 05:54.750
Everyone has the desire and right

05:54.750 --> 05:55.670
to change their fate.

05:56.470 --> 05:58.470
So you support my mom leaving here and going out into the world?

06:03.110 --> 06:04.290
As the head of the family,

06:06.060 --> 06:08.070
I'd rather your mom stay,

06:07.020 --> 06:10.840
♫Beyond the city wall♫

06:09.670 --> 06:11.140
supporting her husband and raising her kid.

06:11.230 --> 06:12.310
It's better for family stability.

06:14.240 --> 06:16.860
But as an elder,

06:14.530 --> 06:20.720
♫From Temple of Cold Hill♫

06:17.790 --> 06:19.590
I also hope she can pursue her dreams.

06:26.480 --> 06:31.210
♫The sound of bells in the midnight♫

06:27.230 --> 06:28.660
My mom once said

06:29.830 --> 06:31.390
she felt suffocated

06:31.390 --> 06:32.750
in this house.

06:35.370 --> 06:36.370
Did she say that to you?

06:37.659 --> 06:38.540
To Granny Ma.

06:37.780 --> 06:42.610
♫Bells break the ship-borne roamer's dream♫

06:40.030 --> 06:41.220
When I was little,

06:41.220 --> 06:43.110
I heard her complaining to Granny Ma.

06:48.000 --> 06:49.600
Now there's less water

06:50.270 --> 06:51.390
in the canal,

06:52.470 --> 06:53.720
and the river has narrowed.

06:54.240 --> 06:56.890
In the past, the canal was full of water,

06:57.270 --> 07:00.680
with many ships and people coming and going. It was so lively.

07:00.880 --> 07:03.010
No matter how good it is, it's just a river, isn't it?

07:03.320 --> 07:04.910
Even a river knows to flow,

07:05.130 --> 07:06.390
let alone people.

07:07.620 --> 07:08.690
Granny Ma.

07:08.710 --> 07:10.520
You've lived here your whole life.

07:10.570 --> 07:11.790
Don't you ever feel stifled?

07:12.670 --> 07:13.560
You know,

07:14.140 --> 07:15.750
I often feel so stifled that

07:15.800 --> 07:17.360
I can barely breathe.

07:18.860 --> 07:20.060
Zhimei.

07:20.410 --> 07:21.870
You've been to big places

07:21.870 --> 07:23.430
and seen the world.

07:23.450 --> 07:26.010
Why don't you talk to Yanlin again

07:26.430 --> 07:28.130
about going out to explore some more?

07:31.190 --> 07:32.409
I don't have the energy to venture out anymore.

07:32.909 --> 07:34.290
As we go through life,

07:34.950 --> 07:36.390
more and more things get in our way and tie us down.

07:38.330 --> 07:39.210
Actually,

07:39.640 --> 07:41.210
even in my dreams,

07:41.460 --> 07:42.710
I think about going out to see the world again,

07:42.909 --> 07:44.020
and to have some more adventure.

07:45.310 --> 07:46.440
But if I leave,

07:46.980 --> 07:48.380
what about this family?

07:48.820 --> 07:50.020
What about the kid?

07:50.700 --> 07:51.670
Alas, life.

07:52.150 --> 07:52.990
It's too difficult.

07:53.940 --> 07:55.130
You're right.

07:55.870 --> 07:57.030
It's not easy.

07:57.800 --> 07:58.980
Since then,

07:59.150 --> 08:00.270
I've been hoping

08:00.470 --> 08:01.520
that my mom could

08:01.870 --> 08:03.810
muster the courage to leave this place one day.

08:06.900 --> 08:08.070
I hope so too.

08:08.790 --> 08:09.590
But

08:11.700 --> 08:13.290
it's tough for your dad.

08:20.480 --> 08:22.380
After all, you have a family.

08:23.290 --> 08:24.810
You have a husband and a kid.

08:25.240 --> 08:26.590
Yet you're constantly

08:26.920 --> 08:28.030
out and about, not coming home.

08:28.320 --> 08:29.970
Don't you think you are being a bit selfish?

08:32.090 --> 08:33.490
Who are you calling selfish?

08:35.409 --> 08:36.909
You're the selfish one, okay?

08:37.630 --> 08:38.549
What did you tell me

08:38.549 --> 08:39.630
when we got married?

08:39.840 --> 08:42.070
You said when the kid got a bit older, you'd have your father take care of him,

08:42.070 --> 08:43.390
and we'd return to Beijing to start our own business.

08:43.429 --> 08:45.280
Have you forgotten what you said yourself?

08:46.200 --> 08:47.390
What's so good about Beijing?

08:47.390 --> 08:49.160
What's not good about Beijing?

08:49.270 --> 08:50.640
Look at Flower Street.

08:50.750 --> 08:51.910
Look at the canal.

08:52.030 --> 08:53.510
How many people are still here?

08:53.640 --> 08:55.170
People always strive for better things.

08:55.620 --> 08:57.480
Big cities offer better opportunities.

08:57.590 --> 08:59.630
Do you know how many ring roads Beijing has built so far?

08:59.630 --> 09:02.060
Even if it had a hundred ring roads, it wouldn't matter to me.

09:02.390 --> 09:04.010
I was born and raised here.

09:04.060 --> 09:05.380
I just like it here.

09:06.030 --> 09:07.080
I think the air here

09:07.150 --> 09:08.180
is better than Beijing's.

09:08.790 --> 09:09.510
Is that not okay?

09:10.740 --> 09:11.670
Since I came back from Beijing,

09:11.710 --> 09:12.830
I've been like a completely different person.

09:12.900 --> 09:14.390
I've also been more energetic here.

09:16.230 --> 09:17.270
Of course you feel different.

09:18.040 --> 09:19.680
It's because you're in your element here.

09:20.950 --> 09:22.770
But what about me?

09:23.420 --> 09:24.830
I'm an actress.

09:24.830 --> 09:26.120
I need a stage.

09:26.510 --> 09:28.070
Is there a stage for me here?

09:29.280 --> 09:31.290
I've been learning opera since I was little.

09:31.630 --> 09:33.070
Opera is particularly demanding.

09:33.500 --> 09:34.900
My teacher said I had no talent.

09:34.940 --> 09:36.470
I was very unwilling to accept that.

09:37.800 --> 09:39.430
I got up at four in the morning every day,

09:39.430 --> 09:41.120
rain or shine, to practice.

09:41.230 --> 09:42.880
I had only one belief in my heart,

09:43.300 --> 09:44.920
and that was to perform on stage.

09:44.990 --> 09:47.030
I have to go on stage no matter where it is!

09:47.190 --> 09:49.420
I want everyone to see me,

09:49.420 --> 09:51.440
to like me and admire me.

09:52.820 --> 09:54.340
As soon as I get on stage,

09:54.840 --> 09:57.020
I want there to be applause and flowers.

09:57.020 --> 09:59.150
Only then would I truly be alive.

09:59.180 --> 10:01.510
Only then could I feel alive.

10:01.590 --> 10:02.870
Do you understand?

10:06.830 --> 10:09.010
You don't understand me at all.

10:25.550 --> 10:26.430
I'm sorry, Zhimei.

10:30.390 --> 10:31.350
I indeed failed to provide you with

10:31.350 --> 10:32.470
a stage that's big enough.

10:40.610 --> 10:41.790
If you feel that

10:44.270 --> 10:45.790
this family is a burden to you,

10:51.900 --> 10:52.950
we can get a divorce.

11:06.780 --> 11:07.470
Let's get divorced.

11:24.080 --> 11:26.480
♫Stepping on the old time♫

11:27.620 --> 11:30.810
♫The wind blows gently♫

11:31.740 --> 11:35.960
♫Blowing through the forest and the city♫

11:37.200 --> 11:39.950
♫Blowing through your face♫

11:40.980 --> 11:43.770
♫And my heart♫

11:45.670 --> 11:48.180
♫The wind blows gently♫

11:46.470 --> 11:47.350
Siyi.

11:47.920 --> 11:48.550
Here.

11:48.730 --> 11:51.610
I made chicken soup for you. Have some.

11:49.270 --> 11:51.540
♫Blowing through summer♫

11:51.860 --> 11:52.910
I'm not hungry yet.

11:52.250 --> 11:54.780
♫Blowing through the eaves♫

11:52.940 --> 11:54.300
Grandma, you eat first.

11:55.810 --> 11:58.010
♫It blows past me♫

11:57.080 --> 11:57.710
Well...

11:58.670 --> 11:59.550
Siyi.

11:58.700 --> 12:02.230
♫Warm love♫

12:00.310 --> 12:01.600
Take a break, will you?

12:03.440 --> 12:04.700
♫How many years♫

12:04.470 --> 12:07.070
I want to discuss something with you.

12:06.040 --> 12:09.140
♫Have you changed?♫

12:08.670 --> 12:09.430
What's wrong, Grandma?

12:09.430 --> 12:10.950
Are you feeling unwell again?

12:10.430 --> 12:12.030
♫How many years♫

12:10.950 --> 12:13.590
No, I'm perfectly fine.

12:12.840 --> 12:15.920
♫How far has the old times♫

12:14.390 --> 12:15.270
Don't be nervous.

12:16.070 --> 12:17.470
I just want to

12:17.230 --> 12:19.010
♫We miss gone♫

12:18.150 --> 12:20.230
talk to you about your mother.

12:19.940 --> 12:23.420
♫I was lost in a distance♫

12:20.790 --> 12:21.550
What about her now?

12:22.630 --> 12:23.870
She came to see me.

12:24.420 --> 12:26.100
♫I couldn't forget♫

12:24.480 --> 12:25.030
She said

12:25.030 --> 12:27.200
she still wanted to go south and explore.

12:26.980 --> 12:30.570
♫The first growth♫

12:27.710 --> 12:30.110
Some of her friends are going with her.

12:30.710 --> 12:31.430
Let her be.

12:31.710 --> 12:33.030
I don't care about her business.

12:35.070 --> 12:36.290
She said

12:36.440 --> 12:38.420
she wanted to let your little brother stay here with us.

12:40.510 --> 12:41.820
Is she crazy?

12:42.030 --> 12:44.350
That boy isn't even related to you by blood.

12:44.420 --> 12:45.740
And he has his own father.

12:46.470 --> 12:47.950
Well, as for Ge,

12:47.950 --> 12:51.440
she said he was arrested and sentenced

12:51.440 --> 12:52.670
for organizing gambling.

12:52.670 --> 12:53.710
And with your mother going south,

12:53.710 --> 12:55.380
there's no one to take care of your little brother.

12:55.380 --> 12:56.790
Then let his own grandmother take care of him.

12:56.790 --> 12:57.710
You're my grandma.

12:57.710 --> 12:59.150
Why should you take care of someone else's grandson?

12:59.150 --> 12:59.950
Do we owe him anything?

13:00.430 --> 13:01.430
It's only for a year.

13:01.670 --> 13:02.950
Not even for a month.

13:02.950 --> 13:04.320
I absolutely disagree with this.

13:05.670 --> 13:06.500
Siyi.

13:07.430 --> 13:09.230
Your mother has had it tough too.

13:09.230 --> 13:11.270
So do I or you have it easy?

13:11.470 --> 13:12.860
She knows very well that I'm preparing for the college entrance exam,

13:12.860 --> 13:13.710
yet she pulls this stunt.

13:13.710 --> 13:14.390
What does she want?

13:14.670 --> 13:16.230
Is she my real mother or not?

13:16.230 --> 13:17.080
Don't yell.

13:17.080 --> 13:18.070
Look at you.

13:18.150 --> 13:20.230
I'm just discussing with you.

13:20.230 --> 13:21.110
Look at us.

13:21.110 --> 13:22.070
We have rent to collect,

13:22.070 --> 13:23.510
and I can work at my stall,

13:23.710 --> 13:24.270
right?

13:24.790 --> 13:26.230
Grandma, you've had a stroke.

13:26.230 --> 13:28.080
How can you still work at the stall?

13:28.270 --> 13:29.860
Kind people are always taken advantage of.

13:30.230 --> 13:32.630
It's not that big a deal. Just an extra pair of chopsticks on the table, right?

13:32.630 --> 13:33.670
It's fine.

13:33.870 --> 13:34.790
It's not fine by me!

13:34.790 --> 13:36.440
I just can't accept it!

13:36.440 --> 13:37.710
She dumped me here with you back then.

13:37.710 --> 13:38.470
All these years, she has barely

13:38.470 --> 13:40.030
ever come back to see me.

13:40.030 --> 13:41.950
How could she have the nerve to ask you this favor?

13:48.830 --> 13:50.070
Siyi.

13:51.670 --> 13:53.070
I'm uneducated,

13:53.070 --> 13:54.750
and I don't know many characters,

13:55.630 --> 13:58.400
but I do know the character for 'person'.

13:59.500 --> 14:01.110
One stroke leans left, and one leans right.

14:01.130 --> 14:03.840
It means a person can't stand alone.

14:03.860 --> 14:06.310
We need to support each other.

14:07.070 --> 14:09.270
Your mother is also unlucky.

14:09.270 --> 14:11.270
When she was little, her brother didn't care for her,

14:11.270 --> 14:12.590
and her mother didn't love her.

14:12.950 --> 14:14.150
She finally married your father,

14:14.150 --> 14:15.870
had a few good years,

14:15.870 --> 14:17.790
but then your father passed away too soon.

14:17.790 --> 14:19.310
You are her own daughter,

14:19.590 --> 14:22.310
and I was once a mother-in-law who loved her.

14:22.310 --> 14:25.150
So tell me, if we don't help her now, who will?

14:25.190 --> 14:26.510
Grandma.

14:30.830 --> 14:32.230
I'm also annoyed with her,

14:34.670 --> 14:36.640
but I have to thank her.

14:37.190 --> 14:39.270
She gave birth to

14:39.300 --> 14:41.720
the best granddaughter in the world.

14:42.170 --> 14:43.530
I owe her.

14:44.120 --> 14:45.200
So I have to pay her back.

14:52.270 --> 14:53.200
Why should we?

15:09.620 --> 15:11.510
Son, I'm home.

15:19.350 --> 15:20.920
Did you bring me a gift?

15:21.510 --> 15:22.920
I was in too much of a hurry this time.

15:22.960 --> 15:23.590
Maybe next time.

15:26.830 --> 15:28.290
When are you leaving?

15:34.150 --> 15:38.070
Aren't you going to Beijing to work?

15:42.280 --> 15:43.770
Your dad told you everything?

15:44.310 --> 15:45.300
No.

15:47.850 --> 15:49.210
You two had a fight,

15:50.190 --> 15:52.060
and I assume it could only be because of this.

16:05.590 --> 16:07.190
I'm not leaving for now.

16:08.710 --> 16:10.290
Not before your college entrance exam.

16:16.850 --> 16:18.700
You should go.

16:19.080 --> 16:20.650
Don't use me as an excuse.

16:21.550 --> 16:24.600
Even if you're here, I won't get into Tsinghua.

16:25.070 --> 16:27.850
And without you here, I won't fail either.

16:29.390 --> 16:31.180
You don't object to my going to Beijing?

16:32.110 --> 16:33.670
You're my mom.

16:34.710 --> 16:36.740
If you're happy, I'm happy.

16:38.420 --> 16:39.620
If you feel suffocated

16:40.550 --> 16:42.070
in this family,

16:42.990 --> 16:44.220
then go somewhere else

16:44.560 --> 16:45.530
and get some fresh air.

16:46.300 --> 16:47.500
Grandpa is right.

16:48.230 --> 16:49.110
Everyone

16:49.410 --> 16:50.510
has the wish and right

16:50.510 --> 16:52.150
to change their own fate.

16:56.190 --> 16:57.590
Thank you, Son.

17:16.140 --> 17:16.810
Mom.

17:20.420 --> 17:21.490
Even if

17:23.490 --> 17:24.230
you two get divorced,

17:27.470 --> 17:28.870
you'll always be my mom.

17:33.630 --> 17:34.790
When I was little,

17:36.180 --> 17:37.290
I was afraid of you leaving

17:38.430 --> 17:40.020
because I feared you would abandon me.

17:41.020 --> 17:42.160
Now,

17:42.980 --> 17:44.030
I've grown up.

17:46.470 --> 17:47.550
So,

17:50.310 --> 17:51.350
feel free to fly, Mom.

17:52.540 --> 17:54.380
Fly to the highest sky.

18:00.630 --> 18:01.810
Thank you, Son.

18:27.830 --> 18:29.190
It's easy to get drunk

18:29.210 --> 18:30.650
drinking alone.

18:31.910 --> 18:32.610
You're off work.

18:42.750 --> 18:44.070
Your wife's back?

18:48.170 --> 18:49.180
But she's leaving again.

18:50.320 --> 18:50.970
Again?

18:51.010 --> 18:51.820
Where to?

18:54.150 --> 18:54.820
Beijing.

18:57.380 --> 18:59.660
She said a film production company

18:59.690 --> 19:00.960
asked her to work there as a producer.

19:02.990 --> 19:04.100
What does a producer do?

19:06.000 --> 19:08.000
In charge of all sorts of things in the production crew, I guess.

19:08.020 --> 19:09.270
I don't know the details.

19:10.340 --> 19:11.650
Can she make money from it?

19:12.980 --> 19:14.730
Our family's problem isn't about money.

19:16.410 --> 19:18.450
So... What is it about?

19:22.450 --> 19:23.220
Let's not talk about it.

19:24.350 --> 19:25.500
I'm filled with anger

19:25.760 --> 19:26.590
that I can't vent.

19:26.590 --> 19:27.480
Come on. Cheers.

19:28.390 --> 19:30.130
The past two years have been suffocating.

19:31.710 --> 19:34.380
I'm also feeling suffocated these days.

19:41.670 --> 19:42.470
What's wrong?

19:43.480 --> 19:44.960
Did something happen to your family too?

19:51.780 --> 19:54.040
You've been to big cities,

19:54.060 --> 19:55.990
and you're more educated than I am.

19:55.990 --> 19:57.430
Help me analyze.

19:58.070 --> 19:58.900
Do you think there's still hope

19:59.470 --> 20:01.380
for this canal?

20:06.420 --> 20:07.250
There is.

20:08.880 --> 20:09.740
How so?

20:12.050 --> 20:13.230
The Grand Canal

20:13.700 --> 20:15.210
is nominated for World Heritage status, you know?

20:16.110 --> 20:18.230
W-What does 'nominated for World Heritage status' mean?

20:19.750 --> 20:20.950
Being nominated for World Heritage status

20:20.970 --> 20:24.820
means it's applying to be included in the World Cultural Heritage Protection List.

20:24.980 --> 20:26.500
Once it makes it onto the list,

20:26.550 --> 20:28.960
the Grand Canal, as a World Cultural Heritage site,

20:28.960 --> 20:30.530
will be protected.

20:30.760 --> 20:32.670
This way, it'll prosper again.

20:34.360 --> 20:35.460
Are you serious?

20:35.480 --> 20:36.340
Of course.

20:37.250 --> 20:38.030
Look.

20:38.150 --> 20:39.090
Last year,

20:39.530 --> 20:40.850
the Grand Canal has already

20:40.870 --> 20:43.450
been included in our country's tentative list for World Heritage nomination.

20:43.990 --> 20:44.710
But of course,

20:45.020 --> 20:46.650
whether the Canal can make it to the final list

20:46.680 --> 20:48.110
depends on our own efforts.

20:50.810 --> 20:51.510
Really?

20:51.660 --> 20:52.330
Sure.

20:53.730 --> 20:54.500
Look.

20:54.570 --> 20:55.990
I'm so lucky to have come to see you

20:56.030 --> 20:57.240
and asked you that question.

20:57.840 --> 20:58.810
Fortunately,

20:58.930 --> 21:00.280
I haven't sold my ship yet.

21:01.930 --> 21:03.350
You'll have to sell that ship of yours.

21:04.550 --> 21:05.310
Why?

21:05.340 --> 21:07.100
Isn't the canal being nominated for World Heritage status?

21:07.120 --> 21:08.910
It's exactly because of the World Heritage nomination.

21:10.190 --> 21:11.520
If it really makes it onto the list,

21:11.550 --> 21:13.040
the Grand Canal will be protected, right?

21:13.110 --> 21:14.910
In the future, ships like yours that burn diesel

21:14.950 --> 21:16.680
and those that cause severe pollution

21:16.720 --> 21:18.150
will all be phased out.

21:19.910 --> 21:21.370
Think about your ship.

21:21.880 --> 21:23.090
It's seven years old.

21:23.730 --> 21:24.740
You still want to keep it?

21:25.270 --> 21:26.030
I'm telling you,

21:26.030 --> 21:27.470
you could be fined to death when the time comes.

21:31.830 --> 21:32.710
I...

21:38.890 --> 21:39.840
This... This...

21:40.490 --> 21:43.040
Boss Xie, I know you feel upset.

21:44.110 --> 21:45.170
I'm upset too.

21:47.660 --> 21:48.660
Look at our Flower Street.

21:48.870 --> 21:50.220
In these past few years,

21:51.540 --> 21:52.890
it's lost its vitality.

21:53.800 --> 21:55.570
Life is getting harder and harder.

21:57.200 --> 21:59.020
But I'm just unwilling to leave.

21:59.550 --> 22:00.670
Do you know why?

22:01.110 --> 22:02.410
Because this is our home.

22:02.440 --> 22:03.440
Our root!

22:04.410 --> 22:05.630
How can I leave, right?

22:18.270 --> 22:18.990
But of course,

22:20.000 --> 22:21.020
as humans,

22:22.430 --> 22:23.940
we must keep up with the times.

22:25.760 --> 22:27.110
So, Boss Xie,

22:28.480 --> 22:29.550
you should come ashore first.

22:30.620 --> 22:32.830
Watch over this Grand Canal,

22:32.830 --> 22:34.430
and wait for it to revive again.

22:34.430 --> 22:35.570
When that day comes,

22:36.440 --> 22:37.670
you can go back to the river.

22:38.910 --> 22:39.880
That'll do, right?

22:53.790 --> 22:55.060
Can we really go back?

23:07.410 --> 23:08.250
Yes, we can.

23:16.780 --> 23:17.870
We can make it back.

24:42.980 --> 24:45.940
[Striving unceasingly with steadfast integrity]

24:43.270 --> 24:46.070
Furthermore, with the general term formula for the geometric sequence,

24:46.070 --> 24:47.270
what can we derive?

24:49.310 --> 24:50.370
Alright, class dismissed.

25:00.020 --> 25:01.740
Let's raise a toast to Liang.

25:01.810 --> 25:02.580
Cheers.

25:02.610 --> 25:04.280
-Come on.
-Let's drink together.

25:05.220 --> 25:06.470
I'm sure everyone will pass.

25:07.750 --> 25:08.810
Come on!

25:08.950 --> 25:10.260
Xie Wanghe!

25:12.950 --> 25:15.280
Xie Wanghe, come on!

25:23.520 --> 25:23.680
[Yunqi Driving School Registration Hall]

25:31.360 --> 25:33.090
She should be able to pass this time.

25:33.310 --> 25:34.700
Right? This should be it.

25:37.240 --> 25:42.200
[Yunqi Driving School Registration Hall]

25:42.380 --> 25:46.250
[Yunqi Driving School Coach Truck]

25:43.490 --> 25:45.550
I think she's definitely going to make it this time.

25:46.700 --> 25:48.300
It's not been easy.

25:47.890 --> 25:55.210
[Yunqi Driving School Coach Truck]

25:49.350 --> 25:50.140
How is it?

25:50.170 --> 25:50.760
No problem.

25:53.180 --> 25:54.000
Thank you.

25:55.630 --> 25:57.430
Well done!

25:57.430 --> 25:58.270
Impressive!

25:58.270 --> 25:58.870
How was it?

25:58.870 --> 25:59.470
Impressive.

25:59.470 --> 26:00.630
I'm the first one to pass, right?

26:00.630 --> 26:01.020
Yes, you are.

26:01.020 --> 26:02.340
Good job.

26:02.860 --> 26:04.040
Good for you, Liang. Well done.

26:04.400 --> 26:05.710
A bet is a bet.

26:05.710 --> 26:06.390
Come on.

26:06.390 --> 26:08.320
Time to pay up. Come on.

26:08.780 --> 26:09.870
Alright, alright.

26:09.870 --> 26:11.470
I was just joking with you guys earlier.

26:11.470 --> 26:12.710
I should be thanking you.

26:12.730 --> 26:14.950
Thank you for taking care of me during this time.

26:15.250 --> 26:16.230
Great job, Liang!

26:16.230 --> 26:17.830
Well done!

26:20.150 --> 26:21.350
Coach Du.

26:22.340 --> 26:23.410
Thank you very much.

26:24.630 --> 26:25.150
Good job.

26:25.200 --> 26:26.470
You passed on the first try.

26:26.630 --> 26:28.510
That's because you taught me well.

26:31.590 --> 26:32.640
Before this,

26:32.870 --> 26:33.860
you really had never learned to drive?

26:35.020 --> 26:37.280
I'm just a quick learner.

26:37.300 --> 26:38.670
If you don't believe me, get a plane.

26:38.690 --> 26:39.530
Let's see

26:39.570 --> 26:41.330
how soon I can learn to fly it.

26:41.350 --> 26:42.360
You're really something.

26:42.460 --> 26:43.320
Liang,

26:43.860 --> 26:44.850
for long-distance driving,

26:45.180 --> 26:46.180
besides the truck,

26:46.310 --> 26:47.990
there's something else you need to prepare.

26:49.320 --> 26:50.150
What is it?

26:57.830 --> 26:58.760
Good to go?

26:59.430 --> 27:00.430
Mr. Chen.

27:00.550 --> 27:02.300
Let me drive. You should get some sleep.

27:02.700 --> 27:03.180
Okay.

27:03.220 --> 27:03.730
Here.

27:13.770 --> 27:14.540
Alright.

28:03.290 --> 28:03.920
Dad.

28:06.380 --> 28:08.190
Can't you drink less?

28:08.270 --> 28:09.840
Your snoring is too loud.

28:11.910 --> 28:13.150
Even your mother can't stop me.

28:13.150 --> 28:14.140
You think you can?

28:15.410 --> 28:17.010
I'm saying this for your own good.

28:17.390 --> 28:18.980
It would be fine if you drink some good liquor,

28:19.000 --> 28:20.480
but what kind of alcohol have you been drinking?

28:21.570 --> 28:22.680
It's bad for your liver.

28:25.870 --> 28:27.100
I feel uncomfortable if I don't drink,

28:28.550 --> 28:29.800
but I feel worse after drinking.

28:35.660 --> 28:37.540
Do you really want to sell that ship?

28:39.290 --> 28:40.180
I do!

28:52.340 --> 28:53.610
Tell me the truth.

28:53.730 --> 28:55.160
If you don't want to sell it,

28:55.950 --> 28:57.070
I'll figure something out and

28:57.370 --> 28:59.090
try my best to keep the boat for you.

29:00.990 --> 29:02.300
I can't keep it anymore.

29:04.150 --> 29:05.030
You know,

29:06.730 --> 29:07.950
one can't fight against fate.

29:12.990 --> 29:13.970
Let me tell you.

29:14.380 --> 29:16.220
Your father is a hero on the river,

29:16.220 --> 29:16.870
but on land,

29:17.810 --> 29:18.690
I'm no coward either.

29:22.070 --> 29:23.450
Alright, let's sell it then.

29:23.880 --> 29:25.710
I've found a buyer for you

29:25.710 --> 29:26.590
online.

29:26.720 --> 29:27.660
120,000.

29:28.680 --> 29:29.710
Really?

29:30.710 --> 29:32.540
The buyer is in Linqing.

29:32.570 --> 29:33.920
He's engaged in earthwork business,

29:34.470 --> 29:35.730
and he's in urgent need of second-hand ships.

29:36.430 --> 29:38.480
There's only one condition:

29:38.900 --> 29:40.050
payment upon delivery of the ship.

29:42.260 --> 29:43.870
But what if he changes his mind

29:43.870 --> 29:45.190
when we deliver the ship there?

29:46.140 --> 29:47.990
I've checked the buyer's transaction history.

29:48.340 --> 29:49.330
Last month alone,

29:49.390 --> 29:51.560
they bought eight second-hand ships.

29:53.320 --> 29:54.910
How about you give it more thought?

29:55.220 --> 29:56.430
If you really decide to sell it,

29:57.480 --> 29:58.730
I'll ask Uncle Xia

29:58.760 --> 29:59.990
to go to Linqing and hand over the ship.

30:22.000 --> 30:29.670
[Smooth Sailing]

30:22.310 --> 30:23.010
Come on.

30:24.150 --> 30:24.800
Come on.

31:09.070 --> 31:12.190
♫Girl, you sit on the bow♫

31:12.190 --> 31:15.230
♫I tow the boat on the shore♫

31:15.230 --> 31:21.070
♫In deep love, tow rope dancing♫

31:47.340 --> 31:50.590
♫Dancing♫

32:51.640 --> 32:52.850
Don't worry, Boss Xie.

33:03.230 --> 33:04.220
Go back.

33:10.020 --> 33:11.280
Go back, Boss Xie.

34:10.370 --> 34:12.929
♫Girl, you sit on the bow♫

34:12.949 --> 34:15.659
♫I tow the boat on the shore♫

34:15.730 --> 34:20.780
♫In deep love, tow rope dancing♫

35:07.950 --> 35:08.830
Have some of this.

35:08.850 --> 35:09.530
Okay.

35:11.130 --> 35:12.060
You don't want some beer?

35:12.060 --> 35:12.910
We have beer.

35:13.140 --> 35:14.810
Beer is perfect for summer.

35:14.840 --> 35:15.770
Come on, come on.

35:15.800 --> 35:16.510
Let's have another bottle.

35:16.510 --> 35:17.230
You're getting more?

35:17.230 --> 35:17.670
Yeah.

35:17.670 --> 35:18.270
There's enough.

35:18.270 --> 35:19.860
Today we must

35:19.890 --> 35:20.960
drink our fill.

35:21.000 --> 35:21.880
Today, this...

35:22.060 --> 35:22.910
Here.

35:22.940 --> 35:24.480
Beers and drinks.

35:24.870 --> 35:25.960
Come on.

35:26.280 --> 35:26.990
Yanlin.

35:27.010 --> 35:28.660
What's the special occasion today?

35:28.660 --> 35:29.710
Everything's so lavish.

35:29.710 --> 35:30.790
There's both wine and meat.

35:30.790 --> 35:32.060
Indeed.

35:32.060 --> 35:33.070
So extravagant.

35:33.070 --> 35:35.270
Boss Xie bought all this meat.

35:35.920 --> 35:37.080
As for the specific reason,

35:37.110 --> 35:38.600
you can ask him yourselves when he comes back.

35:38.620 --> 35:39.820
Is that so?

35:39.870 --> 35:40.670
Let's eat.

35:40.670 --> 35:41.660
Let's help ourselves.

35:41.660 --> 35:42.350
Take it slow.

35:42.350 --> 35:44.470
We should start drinking after Boss Xie comes back.

35:44.470 --> 35:45.510
That's right.

35:45.510 --> 35:46.680
You've started without me?

35:46.760 --> 35:48.280
Boss Xie, you're back.

35:48.430 --> 35:49.390
Come on, have a seat.

35:49.470 --> 35:50.370
Eat.

35:50.390 --> 35:51.430
We were just talking about it.

35:51.430 --> 35:52.630
What's the occasion?

35:52.630 --> 35:54.450
You've bought both wine and meat.

35:54.480 --> 35:56.510
I'll say a few words then.

35:56.540 --> 35:57.470
Um...

35:57.660 --> 35:58.420
Well...

35:58.670 --> 35:59.430
Well...

35:59.450 --> 36:01.230
As you all know, over the past years,

36:02.020 --> 36:03.390
seafaring hasn't been easy.

36:03.580 --> 36:04.900
The longer we stay in the business,

36:04.930 --> 36:05.730
the more we'll lose.

36:06.380 --> 36:07.550
So

36:07.870 --> 36:10.470
my wife and I decided to sell the ship.

36:11.110 --> 36:11.780
We sold it.

36:12.560 --> 36:14.270
But it didn't sell for much.

36:14.540 --> 36:15.580
Only 120,000.

36:15.750 --> 36:16.950
The two of us

36:16.970 --> 36:18.170
thought we'd give

36:18.210 --> 36:20.040
the money to you

36:20.060 --> 36:21.920
according to your share.

36:22.180 --> 36:23.650
Mr. Zhou, here's your share.

36:23.670 --> 36:24.400
Thank you.

36:24.700 --> 36:25.380
Well,

36:25.400 --> 36:27.890
we've calculated carefully.

36:28.570 --> 36:30.890
Plus the dividends from previous years,

36:31.420 --> 36:32.670
fortunately,

36:32.990 --> 36:34.190
you all

36:34.350 --> 36:35.230
didn't lose money in this investment.

36:35.750 --> 36:37.070
Well, that's already a blessing.

36:37.100 --> 36:38.160
That's great.

36:41.610 --> 36:42.660
What about yours?

36:43.690 --> 36:44.470
We...

36:44.470 --> 36:45.510
We won't keep any.

36:45.530 --> 36:46.270
That won't do.

36:46.270 --> 36:47.390
That's not acceptable.

36:47.390 --> 36:49.220
This won't do, Boss Xie.

36:49.220 --> 36:50.750
You've worked the hardest all these years.

36:50.750 --> 36:51.070
That's right.

36:51.070 --> 36:51.990
You were the one taking care of the business.

36:51.990 --> 36:53.610
You're the one who's been making all the money.

36:53.640 --> 36:54.150
Boss Xie.

36:54.190 --> 36:56.230
We all know what kind of person you are.

36:56.250 --> 36:57.170
You are loyal

36:57.200 --> 36:57.880
and dignified.

36:58.170 --> 36:58.880
Everyone knows

36:58.920 --> 37:01.240
you never owe anyone a penny.

37:01.260 --> 37:02.610
You only shortchange yourself.

37:02.630 --> 37:05.330
You've worked extremely hard

37:05.350 --> 37:06.580
for us all these years.

37:06.610 --> 37:08.130
So we can't let your family suffer losses.

37:08.170 --> 37:08.680
That won't do.

37:08.720 --> 37:09.750
Yes, right.

37:09.770 --> 37:10.770
That won't do.

37:10.830 --> 37:11.740
See?

37:11.770 --> 37:12.740
I told you

37:12.770 --> 37:13.820
they'd definitely disagree.

37:14.190 --> 37:15.110
So,

37:15.110 --> 37:15.990
as I said before,

37:16.220 --> 37:17.770
when we make money, everyone's in it together;

37:17.800 --> 37:19.840
and when we lose money, everyone is still in it together.

37:19.860 --> 37:20.340
Right.

37:20.380 --> 37:21.170
Exactly.

37:21.190 --> 37:22.230
It's a business matter after all.

37:22.310 --> 37:23.920
It's about fairness.

37:24.060 --> 37:26.890
The fairest way is to divide the money according to shares.

37:26.910 --> 37:29.020
No more, no less.

37:29.670 --> 37:30.310
As for this money,

37:30.750 --> 37:31.930
we'll take

37:32.370 --> 37:33.070
what belongs to us.

37:33.090 --> 37:34.290
But we won't take

37:35.300 --> 37:36.570
any money that we don't deserve.

37:36.780 --> 37:37.220
That's right.

37:37.240 --> 37:37.900
That's right.

37:37.950 --> 37:39.170
Listen, Boss Xie.

37:39.170 --> 37:40.200
With the two of us here,

37:40.230 --> 37:41.470
it's not your turn to speak.

37:42.060 --> 37:43.310
Here's our family's share.

37:46.080 --> 37:47.620
This... This isn't appropriate.

37:47.640 --> 37:48.470
What's not appropriate?

37:48.470 --> 37:49.260
Exactly.

37:49.260 --> 37:50.430
This really is inappropriate. This...

37:50.450 --> 37:51.370
I agree.

37:52.310 --> 37:53.640
Let's divide the money according to shares.

37:54.060 --> 37:55.620
Those who agree, raise your hands.

37:56.380 --> 37:58.520
♫When the moon hangs in the sky♫

37:58.560 --> 37:59.350
I agree.

37:59.370 --> 38:00.790
We all agree.

38:00.080 --> 38:01.390
♫And it's cooling in the yard♫

38:00.790 --> 38:01.580
I agree.

38:02.440 --> 38:04.880
♫Who is still by your side?♫

38:02.640 --> 38:03.840
We all agree.

38:03.860 --> 38:04.690
I agree.

38:06.750 --> 38:10.450
♫As time passes♫

38:08.230 --> 38:09.110
Agreed. Agreed.

38:09.710 --> 38:12.160
I'd like to thank everyone.

38:11.780 --> 38:15.140
♫Is a lifetime really that long?♫

38:12.180 --> 38:13.180
Thank you all.

38:13.610 --> 38:14.850
Thank you all.

38:15.310 --> 38:16.340
It's only right.

38:16.370 --> 38:19.060
We'll go home and divide it up again.

38:18.510 --> 38:22.050
♫When youthful company fades, leaving only small talk and pleasantries♫

38:19.080 --> 38:19.890
Give us a minute.

38:19.920 --> 38:20.750
Eat first before you go.

38:20.830 --> 38:21.750
Let's eat first.

38:21.750 --> 38:22.590
No, no.

38:22.590 --> 38:23.590
I won't feel at ease until this is sorted out.

38:22.600 --> 38:26.130
♫Spring feels short, while autumn lingers♫

38:23.590 --> 38:24.550
Let's go, Honey.

38:24.770 --> 38:26.460
Then be quick.

38:26.510 --> 38:27.280
Alright, no problem.

38:27.280 --> 38:27.950
Haihong.

38:27.740 --> 38:31.610
♫A gentle breeze carries dreams away♫

38:27.950 --> 38:29.270
Hurry up. We're waiting for you.

38:29.350 --> 38:30.890
We'll wait here to drink with you.

38:31.680 --> 38:33.200
Boss Xie. Boss Xie.

38:32.690 --> 38:36.160
♫Of sweet dreams♫

38:33.440 --> 38:35.670
There's something I'd like to talk to you about.

38:35.670 --> 38:36.700
Go ahead.

38:36.810 --> 38:37.750
Well, earlier,

38:37.750 --> 38:39.990
I forced Maotian to open

38:39.990 --> 38:41.170
that floating supermarket.

38:41.200 --> 38:43.270
It was my fault, not his.

38:41.270 --> 38:44.280
♫Life is long♫

38:43.270 --> 38:44.840
No one's to blame.

38:45.030 --> 38:46.320
As long as it's profitable,

38:45.740 --> 38:48.910
♫No need to dwell♫

38:46.320 --> 38:47.470
it's a good thing.

38:47.620 --> 38:48.590
We've indeed made some

38:48.590 --> 38:49.780
money recently.

38:49.800 --> 38:50.470
Really?

38:50.070 --> 38:53.590
♫Like moonlight♫

38:50.470 --> 38:51.430
That's great.

38:51.950 --> 38:53.190
I wanted to ask,

38:53.190 --> 38:54.630
if you don't mind,

38:54.630 --> 38:56.560
why don't you join us?

38:54.900 --> 38:58.490
♫Don't forget♫

38:58.600 --> 38:59.360
Look.

38:59.390 --> 39:00.640
He has been with you since childhood.

38:59.450 --> 39:02.570
♫Life is long♫

39:00.660 --> 39:02.280
You're his backbone.

39:02.400 --> 39:03.950
Look.

39:04.030 --> 39:04.630
Without you around lately,

39:04.040 --> 39:07.040
♫No need to dwell♫

39:04.740 --> 39:05.640
he's been feeling lost

39:05.680 --> 39:07.270
every day.

39:07.270 --> 39:08.140
Just look at him.

39:08.170 --> 39:09.670
It's like he's lost his soul.

39:09.090 --> 39:12.390
♫Like moonlight♫

39:10.030 --> 39:11.560
So I was thinking,

39:11.890 --> 39:12.810
if you

39:12.830 --> 39:14.350
have nothing else to do,

39:14.000 --> 39:17.570
♫The old times♫

39:14.350 --> 39:16.650
why don't our two families open a floating supermarket together?

39:16.670 --> 39:17.830
We can support each other.

39:17.850 --> 39:18.840
Wouldn't that be great?

39:24.430 --> 39:25.100
Alright.

39:25.750 --> 39:27.110
So it's a deal.

39:27.320 --> 39:28.290
I'm off then.

39:29.480 --> 39:30.270
Have some.

39:30.270 --> 39:31.150
Eat it while it's warm.

39:32.680 --> 39:33.910
In the future, if there's anything you want to say,

39:33.940 --> 39:35.530
talk to me yourself, okay?

39:36.030 --> 39:37.550
Having your wife relay messages for you?

39:37.590 --> 39:38.630
Is this how you do things now?

39:38.470 --> 39:40.290
♫When the moon hangs in the sky♫

39:40.920 --> 39:42.390
♫And it's cooling in the yard♫

39:41.050 --> 39:42.000
Go on. I'll be there right away.

39:42.030 --> 39:42.660
Okay.

39:43.500 --> 39:45.840
♫Who is still by your side?♫

39:45.430 --> 39:46.590
Let's start dividing the dividends.

39:47.860 --> 39:51.330
♫As time passes♫

39:52.710 --> 39:56.150
♫Is a lifetime really that long?♫

39:54.340 --> 39:55.670
Tell me, why do they

39:55.670 --> 39:57.190
like seafaring so much?

39:57.920 --> 39:59.580
I went seafaring with them a few times,

39:59.600 --> 40:03.050
♫When youthful company fades, leaving only small talk and pleasantries♫

39:59.940 --> 40:01.210
but I didn't find it that enjoyable.

40:02.750 --> 40:03.590
Maybe

40:03.790 --> 40:07.250
♫Spring feels short, while autumn lingers♫

40:04.550 --> 40:06.370
they were born in the year of the fish in their previous life.

40:07.020 --> 40:07.990
That's it?

40:08.930 --> 40:12.700
♫A gentle breeze carries dreams away♫

40:10.510 --> 40:12.110
She drove me out.

40:12.150 --> 40:12.800
Boss Xie.

40:12.800 --> 40:14.130
She said I'm innumerate.

40:13.810 --> 40:17.840
♫Dreamland and dreams♫

40:14.860 --> 40:16.780
Come on.

40:17.170 --> 40:19.100
Seafaring used to be a good profession.

40:19.590 --> 40:20.430
They used to make good money from it,

40:20.430 --> 40:21.190
and they enjoyed the freedom.

40:21.800 --> 40:23.650
People would carry things

40:22.270 --> 40:25.300
♫Life is long♫

40:23.830 --> 40:25.630
to their homes, begging them to make a trip.

40:26.270 --> 40:27.750
In that era of insufficient transportation capacity,

40:26.730 --> 40:29.710
♫No need to dwell♫

40:28.400 --> 40:30.320
ship owners could walk with their heads held high.

40:30.340 --> 40:31.780
So during that period,

40:31.480 --> 40:34.820
♫Like moonlight♫

40:32.340 --> 40:34.390
they felt respected and needed.

40:35.370 --> 40:36.110
Unfortunately,

40:36.460 --> 40:39.940
♫Don't forget♫

40:36.540 --> 40:37.680
times have changed.

40:38.510 --> 40:40.340
But they're still living in the past,

40:40.990 --> 40:43.590
in the glory and honor of the old times.

40:41.250 --> 40:44.160
♫Life is long♫

40:45.700 --> 40:48.640
♫No need to dwell♫

40:48.600 --> 40:49.960
Seeing them like this,

40:49.990 --> 40:51.030
I feel discouraged too.

40:50.710 --> 40:53.890
♫Like moonlight♫

40:52.170 --> 40:54.350
I want to help, but I'm at a loss.

40:54.840 --> 40:56.180
I feel really bad.

40:55.540 --> 40:58.760
♫The old times♫

40:57.210 --> 40:59.290
Then work hard and improve yourself.

40:59.910 --> 41:02.230
Make them proud of you.

41:03.580 --> 41:05.380
Maybe you can do it, but I can't.

41:06.510 --> 41:07.790
Why can't you?

41:08.750 --> 41:09.480
Fenghua.

41:10.820 --> 41:12.460
You have an advantage that others don't have.

41:12.990 --> 41:13.890
What?

41:13.990 --> 41:14.870
You're thick-skinned.

41:16.750 --> 41:17.870
I'm serious.

41:19.060 --> 41:20.560
Look at other girls.

41:20.880 --> 41:21.960
They're all pretentious

41:21.990 --> 41:23.190
and aren't sincere at all.

41:23.220 --> 41:24.160
But you're different.

41:24.550 --> 41:26.190
You've been very genuine since you were little.

41:26.190 --> 41:27.400
You are what you are,

41:27.400 --> 41:28.390
never pretending.

41:28.570 --> 41:30.080
With your personality,

41:30.550 --> 41:32.190
when you do things in the future,

41:32.190 --> 41:34.230
you'll be more easily accepted by clients,

41:34.250 --> 41:35.920
and it'll be easier for you to make friends.

41:36.190 --> 41:37.940
You just lack experience now.

41:38.550 --> 41:39.840
When you figure out

41:39.840 --> 41:41.030
what you want to do in the future,

41:41.660 --> 41:42.710
you'll have an advantage.

41:42.730 --> 41:44.320
You'll be faster than others

41:44.360 --> 41:46.200
in gaining resources and connections.

41:49.270 --> 41:50.430
Are you serious?

41:50.430 --> 41:51.700
Don't lie to me.

41:51.700 --> 41:53.390
Of course. Why would I lie to you?

41:54.110 --> 41:55.300
You know what?

41:55.660 --> 41:57.270
When you come to Beijing in the future, come work with me.

41:57.710 --> 41:59.010
It's not because we're close,

41:59.120 --> 42:01.110
but because I think you have potential.

42:10.190 --> 42:11.790
Then what about Siyi?

42:14.760 --> 42:15.780
Her?

42:17.170 --> 42:18.770
With her personality,

42:18.880 --> 42:20.250
she's suitable for academic work,

42:20.260 --> 42:21.300
not for starting a business.

42:23.030 --> 42:25.630
Will she be in your future?

42:29.470 --> 42:30.230
What do you mean?

42:32.790 --> 42:34.230
You won't start a business with her,

42:34.260 --> 42:36.000
but what about other things?

42:36.180 --> 42:37.570
What other things?

42:39.720 --> 42:42.230
Like relationship and such.

42:52.590 --> 42:53.490
Fenghua.

42:53.630 --> 42:55.410
You watch too many soap operas.

42:55.770 --> 42:57.190
Your IQ is not high in the first place.

42:57.190 --> 42:59.110
You'll become an idiot if you keep watching them.

43:03.110 --> 43:04.030
Who are you talking about?

43:04.030 --> 43:04.830
Say that again.

43:04.830 --> 43:06.070
-Who are you calling an idiot?
-I'm wrong. I'm wrong.

43:06.190 --> 43:07.990
-Are you wrong or not?
-I am. I am.
